WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.079 --> 00:00:04.350
From pet monkeys, to ice picks and stolen
peaches,

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:09.210
Sarah Paulson's super-stylish Nurse Ratched
has arrived on Netflix taking us on a dark

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:13.219
horror-filled tour of the American psychiatric
care system.

00:00:13.219 --> 00:00:16.710
Yippee-ki-yay movie lovers,
I'm Jan and in this video we're taking a deep

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:21.080
dive into Ratched Season 1,
the ending and the 4-season arc planned for

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:23.789
the series,
plus I'll point out some cool details you

00:00:23.789 --> 00:00:25.010
might have missed.

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:27.630
Spoilers ahead, so take care if you haven't
seen the show yet.

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:32.930
In terms of Ratched's brother Edmund, by the
end of the final episode, he and Mildred have

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:34.729
become enemies.

00:00:34.729 --> 00:00:38.870
Edmund's botched attempt at escape with Dolly
put him under a stricter lockdown when he

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:42.340
was recaptured,
and with an excruciating death awaiting him

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:46.180
in the electric chair,
Mildred decides to secretly euthanise him

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:47.180
herself.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:51.840
But when Charlotte Wells, now in her Dr Hanover
persona, breaks him out, he discovers his

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:54.760
sister's plan, which turns him against her.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:58.050
With no other way out,
obviously Mildred's intention was to stop

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:01.320
him suffering an agonising death in the electric
chair,

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:05.330
but Edmund doesn't see it that way,
even though he himself was to blame for screwing

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:09.540
up their original plan to get him off the
death sentence at the Spring dance.

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:13.500
On top of that, Edmund still seems to blame
Mildred for running when he murdered their

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:17.430
abusive foster parents, even though he told
her to leave.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:22.480
So when Edmund reveals he massacred seven
nurses in Chicago, Mildred understands he's

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:28.130
coming for her, thus setting him up to be
her primary antagonist in Season 2.

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:32.340
And given that Dolly shot Gwen during her
and Edmund's escape, I think it's possible

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:36.970
that he could try and hurt his sister by targeting
Gwendolyne as well.

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:41.890
If Edmund does end up killing Gwen, this could
be particularly traumatic for Mildred, given

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:45.659
how she helped her accept her sexuality and
learn how to love.

00:01:45.659 --> 00:01:48.970
"My feelings for you are the truest thing
in me.

00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:50.200
I love you."

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:55.320
Gwen's death might be what sets Mildred off
down an even darker and more repressive path

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:57.670
again,
taking her closer to the cold and hardened

00:01:57.670 --> 00:02:01.049
character of Nurse Ratched we see in One Flew
Over The Cuckoo's Nest,

00:02:01.049 --> 00:02:02.960
which this series is a prequel to.

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:07.640
As for Edmund's ultimate fate, there could
be a clue in the way the TV show seems to

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:12.080
present some parallels between him and Jack
Nicholson's character Randle in the movie.

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:15.640
For example, in the opening scene of the first
episode,

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:19.820
Edmund wears a leather jacket and green T-shirt
similar to Randle's leather jacket that he

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:24.200
wears when we he arrives at the hospital and
also his green T-shirt.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:28.130
There's also the way that Edmund tries to
fake that he's insane to make sure that he

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:31.320
doesn't stand trial,
which is similar to how Nicholson's Randle

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:36.410
pretended to be mentally ill in the movie
to get out of doing hard labour in prison.

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:41.700
And by the end of Season 1, Edmund is now
Mildred's primary antagonist, just like Randle

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:44.900
became Nurse Ratched's principal adversary
in the movie.

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:48.990
So, given Mildred tells Edmund, that she's
the one who'll be coming after him,

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:53.360
I wonder whether he'll end up captured by
Mildred and then lobotomised to neutralise

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:57.190
the threat he poses to her,
similar to what happened to Randle in Cuckoo's

00:02:57.190 --> 00:03:00.590
Nest,
and ironically similar to how Mildred originally

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:04.810
saved Edmund from the surviving priest's eye-witness
testimony.

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:10.500
And in her eyes, Mildred might even see lobotomising
Edmund as an act of mercy of sorts so that

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:13.980
he can no longer continue his murderous ways.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:18.080
What's interesting about how the first season
of Ratched ends is the extent to which Mildred

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:22.569
subverts our expectations of her based on
how she was initially depicted in the season's

00:03:22.569 --> 00:03:23.860
early episodes.

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:28.140
In Mildred's opening scene in the Pilot,
we get a sense of her brooding darkness and

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:32.090
inner repression as she watches a couple engaged
in heavy PDA,

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:36.790
then proceeds to scold a distracted gas attendant
about his filthy fingernails.

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:41.260
We then watch her lie her way into a nurse's
position at Lucia State Hospital where she

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:45.930
encourages a patient's suicide which she then
helps Dr Hanover cover up.

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:50.290
Using this as leverage, she has him make her
head nurse, taking over from Nurse Bucket.

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:54.849
And there's an interesting detail which foreshadows
the way Mildred quickly insinuates herself

00:03:54.849 --> 00:03:59.940
into this position of power when Bucket brings
some lilies of the valley into Hanover's office.

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:05.050
The lily of the valley is a species of flower
that spreads aggressively and which is toxic,

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:06.370
sometimes lethal.

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:11.120
Already by the second episode, we see how
Mildred is excited to observe Dr Hanover's

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:15.590
demonstration of the lobotomy procedure on
four newly arrived patients,

00:04:15.590 --> 00:04:19.019
and with her passive-aggressive threats against
anyone who wrongs her,

00:04:19.019 --> 00:04:23.610
it sets us up to assume she'll be travelling
down a progressively darker path as the season

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:24.610
goes on.

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:25.610
"What are you gonna do about it?

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:26.610
What are you, deaf?"

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:27.610
"No.

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:29.400
I'm just thinking of all the things I'm going
to do about it."

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:34.680
Which is why it feels surprising when Mildred
turns compassionate towards Betsy after she's

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:37.889
rejected by Dr Hanover at the Spring dance.

00:04:37.889 --> 00:04:42.240
Despite the evidence of a more human side,
Mildred clearly has this dark underbelly and

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:45.640
admits to Gwen that she holds no regrets for
everything she's done.

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:46.640
"The lies I told to get into that hospital,
to get closer to Edmund...

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:50.339
Those were amoral acts, and I understand that
completely, but you must understand that I

00:04:50.339 --> 00:04:51.819
had no choice.

00:04:51.819 --> 00:04:54.939
And if I had to, I would do it all over again."

00:04:54.939 --> 00:05:00.379
Speaking to Vanity Fair, Sarah Paulson said
that she identifies "very deeply with [Mildred's]

00:05:00.379 --> 00:05:02.729
loneliness"
and thinks that what drives her character

00:05:02.729 --> 00:05:06.180
is "a pursuit of survival and of finding some
sense of home.

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:12.169
[It's] sort of an animal need that blinds
her to the inappropriateness of some her actions."

00:05:12.169 --> 00:05:16.550
A character who we may see return in the second
season is the odious Henry,

00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:21.169
the son of Miss Osgood who according to his
mother's will finds himself disinherited and

00:05:21.169 --> 00:05:25.479
destined to be sent to a psychiatric institution
at the end of Season 1.

00:05:25.479 --> 00:05:29.249
It's not hard to think that he'll probably
end up at Lucia State Hospital,

00:05:29.249 --> 00:05:32.949
where he might try to manipulate any of the
nurses looking after him,

00:05:32.949 --> 00:05:36.990
similar to how he had his mother brutally
killed by one of his servants.

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:40.889
And if Henry discovers it was Mildred who
was paid a large bounty from his mother in

00:05:40.889 --> 00:05:44.729
return for Dr Hanover's head,
then he might try and blackmail her;

00:05:44.729 --> 00:05:49.909
though I can't imagine the outcome would be
favourable for him if he gets on her bad side.

00:05:49.909 --> 00:05:54.189
By the way, there was an intriguing detail
I noticed in the scene when Mildred presents

00:05:54.189 --> 00:05:56.759
Miss Osgood with Dr Hanover's head.

00:05:56.759 --> 00:06:01.250
The painting that's positioned perfectly between
the two women is Salome with the decapitated

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:03.219
head of John the Baptist.

00:06:03.219 --> 00:06:07.830
Like Miss Osgood, who requested Dr Hanover's
head as revenge for his part in her son losing

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:12.569
his limbs, in the Bible Salome requested the
head of John be brought to her as vengeance

00:06:12.569 --> 00:06:14.869
on behalf of her mother.

00:06:14.869 --> 00:06:19.399
Another way that Mildred rationalises both
her good and bad actions is through the idea

00:06:19.399 --> 00:06:21.449
that she's an "angel of mercy".

00:06:21.449 --> 00:06:25.800
This theme first came up in the pilot episode:
"I admire nurses more than anything.

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:27.659
They really are God's angels."

00:06:27.659 --> 00:06:28.659
"Yes.

00:06:28.659 --> 00:06:29.659
Yes, we are."

00:06:29.659 --> 00:06:33.669
This is developed further in the two "Angel
of Mercy" episodes where Huck calls Mildred

00:06:33.669 --> 00:06:38.149
by that name after she helps two patients
escape so they no longer have to undergo the

00:06:38.149 --> 00:06:42.800
cruel hydrotherapy treatments,
a form of conversion therapy designed to supposedly

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:44.050
eradicate their lesbianism.

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:45.050
"You're an angel.

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:46.659
What you did for those women.

00:06:46.659 --> 00:06:48.689
Mildred Ratched...
you're an angel of mercy."

00:06:48.689 --> 00:06:52.849
Then there are the flashbacks to Ratched's
time as a nurse during the war, when she would

00:06:52.849 --> 00:06:58.020
frequently euthanise severely wounded soldiers
who asked her to put them out of their misery.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:01.419
The term "angel of mercy" also has multiple
layers of meaning.

00:07:01.419 --> 00:07:05.919
It's sometimes used as a nickname for nurses
in general, with Florence Nightingale being

00:07:05.919 --> 00:07:09.339
one of the first nurses who was dubbed an
"angel of mercy".

00:07:09.339 --> 00:07:11.520
And then there's the criminological use of
the term,

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:15.869
where it refers to serial killers,
frequently caregivers who decide to kill their

00:07:15.869 --> 00:07:20.429
patients whether it be for compassionate or
sadistic reasons rather than treat them.

00:07:20.429 --> 00:07:24.909
I also noticed the artwork on the Netflix
page for Ratched has Rorschach-test inkblots

00:07:24.909 --> 00:07:29.930
positioned behind Mildred that give the impression
of angel wings emerging from behind her.

00:07:29.930 --> 00:07:34.490
Ratched also perceives herself as an angel
of mercy, believing that she's helping some

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:37.469
of her victims find peace from their suffering.

00:07:37.469 --> 00:07:40.419
"You have been subjected to enough pain.

00:07:40.419 --> 00:07:43.979
You deserve someone to show you mercy, Mr.
Salvatore."

00:07:43.979 --> 00:07:48.860
Engineering Salvatore's suicide was, of course,
self-serving for Mildred, but an even more

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:53.740
shocking example of how she can quickly switch
between compassion and brutality is in the

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:55.020
fourth episode.

00:07:55.020 --> 00:07:58.520
In the course of one evening,
Mildred helps Ingrid and Lily escape their

00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:03.830
shockingly painful hydrotherapy treatments,
but at the same time with the help of Dr Hanover,

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:08.119
she locks Charles Wainwright into one of the
tanks and turns the temperature up to a level

00:08:08.119 --> 00:08:09.749
that will boil him alive.

00:08:09.749 --> 00:08:13.990
Getting rid of Charles is not only expedient
as it's yet another death on the hospital

00:08:13.990 --> 00:08:18.639
premises that Mildred can hold over Hanover,
but it's also a form of revenge for the poor

00:08:18.639 --> 00:08:20.439
way Charles treated her.

00:08:20.439 --> 00:08:25.539
The series really whipsaws us in the way we
often simultaneously see cruelty and kindness

00:08:25.539 --> 00:08:26.539
in Mildred.

00:08:26.539 --> 00:08:31.289
At the same time that she and Betsy conspire
to turn Dr Hanover in to the authorities,

00:08:31.289 --> 00:08:36.349
she kindly asks Bucket to make Huck head nurse,
because she knew he was suffering from a feeling

00:08:36.349 --> 00:08:38.280
of lack of purpose in his life.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:42.690
The reveal of her dreadful childhood also
makes her more sympathetic.

00:08:42.690 --> 00:08:47.400
Mildred is most definitely a complicated but
intriguing character and Gwendolyne expresses

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:51.400
how she and perhaps many viewers may feel
about her when she says:

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:54.460
"I don't understand how I got so...
tangled up in you."

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:58.330
That's also a nice reference to the opening
title sequence for the series in which we

00:08:58.330 --> 00:09:04.370
see characters chasing and pulling on a tangled
red string that leads to Nurse Ratched.

00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:08.910
Something that's also a major theme in the
first season of Ratched is the idea of image,

00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:12.710
façade, and fantasy;
in particular our protagonist Mildred who

00:09:12.710 --> 00:09:16.690
presents herself as the image of a perfect
nurse while also dressed to the nines.

00:09:16.690 --> 00:09:21.670
However, this is a false image or façade
as Mildred never trained as a nurse and lied

00:09:21.670 --> 00:09:25.900
her way into the army,
falsified her interview letter with Dr Hanover,

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:29.550
her clothes are stolen,
and despite her lesbian fantasies, she tries

00:09:29.550 --> 00:09:34.460
to repress these feelings by having sex with
Charles Wainwright and uses roleplays to get

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:35.570
through this.

00:09:35.570 --> 00:09:40.210
There's also the hospital itself which is
decked out like a luxury hotel despite being

00:09:40.210 --> 00:09:43.190
financially on the brink of closing down.

00:09:43.190 --> 00:09:46.860
Numerous other characters also live in their
own fantasy worlds.

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:51.990
Dolly sees herself as a kind of movie star
and romanticises her escape with serial killer

00:09:51.990 --> 00:09:52.990
Edmund.

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:54.130
"This is killer-diller good luck.

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:55.570
Like Bonnie and Clyde."

00:09:55.570 --> 00:10:00.280
This fantasy leads to a tragic end for her
though, because similar to Bonny and Clyde,

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:04.120
Dolly gets herself killed when the pair are
discovered by the police.

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:08.770
Betsy Bucket also has a misguided belief or
fantasy that Dr Hanover actually cares for

00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:11.420
her, when in reality he can't stand her.

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:16.210
And he himself is living a double-life, hiding
from his past and his disaster with Miss Osgood's

00:10:16.210 --> 00:10:17.490
son Henry.

00:10:17.490 --> 00:10:22.800
Tragically, and perhaps ironically,
Dr Hanover ends up killed by his patient Charlotte

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:26.910
Wells when her psyche breaks and she takes
on one of her fantasy personas,

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:28.850
believing Hanover to be Adolf Hitler.

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:33.580
That personality is based on Jesse Owens,
the African American athlete who won four

00:10:33.580 --> 00:10:38.580
gold medals at the 1936 Berlin Olympic Games
in Nazi Germany.

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:42.940
In contrast to the others living in a fantasy,
the main character who deals with things in

00:10:42.940 --> 00:10:45.270
a much more straightforward way is Huck.

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:50.230
Huck is damaged too, but his character's wounds
are more external rather than internalised

00:10:50.230 --> 00:10:51.880
like many of the others.

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:56.400
And for me, I was gutted when he was killed
as he felt like one of the only truly decent

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:58.370
characters in the show.

00:10:58.370 --> 00:11:02.500
If you're wondering about how long Ratched
will run for, well, Ryan Murphy apparently

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:07.840
has four seasons mapped out, each one featuring
a different male adversary for Mildred.

00:11:07.840 --> 00:11:12.230
For Season 1, this was Dr Hanover, and it
looks like Edmund will be her main antagonist

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:13.710
in the second season.

00:11:13.710 --> 00:11:18.430
Sarah Paulson has also said that by the fourth
season she expects the show to be in the events

00:11:18.430 --> 00:11:22.560
of One Flew Over The Cuckoo's Nest, so that
could mean we'll see Randle McMurphy show

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:24.280
up to oppose Mildred.

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:28.850
I expect if that happens, there will a few
changes to the story from the film, in a similar

00:11:28.850 --> 00:11:33.980
way to how Bates Motel modified some of the
events from Psycho in its final season.

00:11:33.980 --> 00:11:37.440
So, what did you think about the first season
of Ratched?

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:41.480
And do you have any predictions or things
you'd like to see in the second season?

00:11:41.480 --> 00:11:43.480
Leave your thoughts in the comments below.

00:11:43.480 --> 00:11:47.960
If you enjoyed this, don't forget to leave
a thumbs-up and subscribe for all my upcoming

00:11:47.960 --> 00:11:48.960
videos.

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:53.290
Tap left for my next Netflix video or tap
right for something else you're sure to like.

00:11:53.290 --> 00:11:55.400
Thanks for watching and see ya next time.

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:56.610
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

